      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bowe Property presents to the market a most interesting and versatile agricultural land holding of approximately 14 acres (5.73 hectares) of excellent agricultural quality, within a most convenient location just 2.8kms from Innishannon, 2.2kms from Crossbarry and 19kms south-west of Cork City. The lands are all under grass, with clearly defined natural boundaries and a pleasant, reasonably level topography. The lands lend themselves ideally as additional acreage to any farming enterprise, and qualifying candidates may be attracted by the potential to secure planning under rural housing control zoning for a private residence (S.P.P.). The lands are offered for immediate sale with full vacant possession and are contained in Folio CK3207. Maps and further details are available by contacting Brendan Bowe of Bowe Property on 087 259 4481."
      }
